    LLM: 'Game: Golf. Objective: Have the lowest scoring layout at the end of each hole (hand).',
    Player: 'Golf: play by the rules, manage scoring opportunities, and pursue the win condition.',
    objective: 'Have the lowest scoring layout at the end of each hole (hand). Play 9 or 18 holes; lowest cumulative score wins.',
    gameplay: 'FOUR-CARD GOLF:\n1. Players arrange 4 cards face down in square; view 2 nearest cards once\n2. Player left of dealer starts\n3. On your turn, either: - Draw from stock, optionally replace a layout card (discard replaced card) - Take top discard, must use to replace layout card - Knock (ends play after others take one more turn)\n4. Cannot look at layout cards before deciding which to replace\n5. If you look at a face-down card, you must replace it SIX-CARD GOLF:\n1. 6 cards arranged 2x3, usually all face down initially\n2. Draw and replace as in 4-card\n3. Replacement cards placed face up\n4. Play ends when one player has all cards face up',
    keyRules: [
      'You cannot look at your face-down cards before deciding which to replace',
      'If you draw from stock, you may discard it without using it',
      'If you take the discard, you must use it to replace a card',
      'In 4-card, knocking ends the hand',
      'In 6-card, play ends when one player has all cards face up',
      'Looking at a face-down card forces you to replace it',
    ],
